                    <msContents>
                        <summary>
                            <p>The two MSS. Supp. 8 and Supp. 9 are Nos. 9 and 10 in a volume of miscellanea, which also
                                contains the following printed or lithographed items: (1) Le Fars (Tihrán,
                                June, 1913); (2) speech of the Náşiru'l-Mulk on assuming the Regency on
                                12 Safar, 1329/Feb. 12, 1911, and telegrams from the Mujtahids, etc.,
                                connected therewith; (3) Persian and Turkish poems of Lá'lí of Tabríz; (4)
                                al-Islám (lith.), No. 7 of First Year, Tihrán, 18 Rabí' I, 1332/Feb. 14, 1914;
                                (5) al-Maqádu'l-Asná (printed), on Double Entry, Tihrán, Jumádà I, 1323/
                                July, 1905; and (6)-(8) three Persian Almanacs, for 1326/1908-9, 1323/1905-6
                                and 1318/1900-1, lithographed at Tihrán. None of these eight printed/
                                lithographed items has its own Fihrist classmark in this record.</p> 
                            <p>Sup. 9 (the tenth item in the volume) was also received from Mr H. L. Rabino,
                                with a letter of the same date (April 11, 1914). Mr Rabino describes it as "a few
                                leaves from the draft of Mírzá Ibráhím's journal of his journey with Captain
                                Mackenzie, British Consul in Rasht (Persia), in 1859." Melgunov's book Das
                                südliche Ufer des Kaspischen Meeres is based on it. Ff. 19 of 17.5 x 10 cm and 14
                                to 16 ll. Written in ním-shikasta.</p>
                            <p>In the lettering on the back of the volume these two MSS. are described
                                respectively as "MS. Journal of Travel in Caspian Provinces" and "Kitábcha-i-
                                Langarúd."</p>
                        </summary> 
                        <msItem xml:id="Supp_9-item1">
                            <author key="person_f3040" cert="medium">
                                <persName xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc">Mírzá Ibráhím</persName>
                            </author>
                            <title xml:lang="en" type="desc" key="">Journal of Travel in Caspian Provinces</title>
                            <title xml:lang="en" type="desc">Draft of a journal of a journey with
                                Captain Mackenzie, British Consul in Rasht, in 1859</title>
                            <note>A few leaves only. Described by Rabino as the source for
                                Mel'gunov's book Das südliche Ufer des Kaspischen Meeres. Lettered
                                on the spine of the bound volume as "MS. Journal of Travel in
                                Caspian Provinces."</note>
                            <textLang mainLang="fa">Persian</textLang>
